# Example ReRDMFT input file: water molecule, DEBUG TRUE with VERBOSE 2
# -- on top of everything VERBOSE 1 already runs (see
# water_debug_verbose1.inp), this also validates the MIXED real/
# imaginary orbital-rotation Hessian block (Hessian_opt/
# HartreeExchangeHessian.h's hartreeExchangeHessianElementMixed,
# Hess^ty_pq,rs = d^2E/dt_pq dy_rs) against a genuine mixed-direction
# 2D finite difference (a real step on one orbital-rotation pair
# crossed with an imaginary step on another) -- only meaningful for
# C4_SPINOR's genuinely complex spinors, and a newer, less commonly
# needed check than everything else DEBUG/VERBOSE 1 already cover, so
# it needs a strictly higher VERBOSE threshold (> 1, not just > 0).
NELEC 10
BASIS water-sto-3g.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
DEBUG TRUE
VERBOSE 2

GEOMETRY
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.757000   0.586000
H   0.000000  -0.757000   0.586000
END
